  "id": "conceptual-imagery",
  "term": "conceptual imagery",
  "definition": "Conceptual imagery is the mental representation of a concept that may arise after language has already been processed. In this context, it refers to a possible indirect route by which motor brain structures become active after understanding language, rather than being recruited directly by language processing itself.",
